$ varag run --help
# started 2026-10-21T08:05:45.064+00:00
Usage: varag run [OPTIONS]

  Generate, execute in both environments, write results and traces.

Options:
  --methods TEXT                  Comma-separated method ids or all.
                                  [default: all]
  --model TEXT                    Backend id from configs/models.yaml.
                                  [required]
  --split [dev|test|all]          [default: dev]
  --user-arm [knows|unsure|leak_audit]
                                  leak_audit: every question is replaced by an
                                  irrelevant one (the leak audit only).
  --limit INTEGER                 Only the first N instances (parsing checks
                                  with cpu_tiny).
  --instances FILE                A file of instance ids, one per line: run
                                  only those (the serving-noise subset).
  --fresh-cache                   Use a cache private to this run: every
                                  request reaches the server (serving-noise
                                  check).
  --max-usd FLOAT                 Spending cap: refuse to start when the
                                  estimate exceeds it, stop when the running
                                  total reaches it.
  --repeats INTEGER               Repeat indices 0..N-1 per (instance,
                                  method); default the backend's `repeats` in
                                  configs/models.yaml.
  --help                          Show this message and exit.
